## Fixtures (visualization — `spec/core/code.md` §10.1)

Per §10.1.1, every well-formed CX program MUST be renderable to a
sequence/activity diagram per the locked rendering rules in §10.1.2,
and every diagram produced by a conforming renderer MUST round-trip:
reverse-parse back to a CX tree that is `cx-diff`-equal to the source.

The Phase 4 reference renderer's three output formats (SVG / PNG /
Mermaid) all feed through the same reverse-parse path. Gate #9 (per
§11.6 test gates) tests structural equality at the *tree* level, not
the SVG-bytes level — so each fixture below pins down the **canonical
CX tree** the renderer's reverse-parse MUST produce, exercising one
row of the §10.1.2 rendering table.

`in_code` is the source program (the diagram's forward-render input);
`out_text` is the canonical CX form the reverse-parse MUST yield (which
for a well-formed program is the source program echoed in canonical
form per `spec/core/canonical.md`). The runner (Phase 4 deliverable; harness
`vcx/tests/runners/cxl_diagram_roundtrip.v` per §11.4.2 gate-9
protocol) renders to each of {svg, png, mermaid}, reverse-parses each
back to a CX tree, and asserts structural equality with the canonical
form below under `cx-diff`.

Until the Phase 4 renderer ships, these fixtures are parse-only — the
existing `vcx/tests/code_parse_fixtures_test.v` confirms each
`in_code` parses cleanly under the v0.8.0 grammar, which is the
prerequisite for renderability per §10.1.1.
#]]
 ]

