## Modify fixture status — supported vs deferred (2026-05-23)

The v0.8.0 `[?modify]` evaluator (ba5a6e4c / 846e0114) wires the
following fixtures cleanly against the reference impl:

| Fixture | Status |
|---|---|
| `program-modify-002-delete-node` | ✅ supported |
| `program-modify-004-no-match-returns-unchanged` | ✅ supported |
| `program-modify-005-using-transform` | ✅ supported (un-deferred 2026-05-23 — uses `[cast $p :int]`) |
| `program-modify-006-set-attr` | ✅ supported |
| `program-modify-007-rename` | ✅ supported (renderer body-text quoting fix, task #43) |
| `program-modify-008-append-child` | ✅ supported (renderer body-text quoting fix, task #43) |
| `program-modify-string-scalar-roundtrip` | ✅ supported (regression — task #43) |
| `program-modify-path-modifier-disambig-1` | ✅ supported |
| `program-modify-path-modifier-disambig-2` | ✅ supported (genuine prefix:local) |
| `program-modify-path-modifier-disambig-3` | ✅ supported (predicate-then-modifier) |

The former three deferred fixtures (001 / 003 / 009) are now **resolved
2026-05-30** under the attribute-axis lock (design (a), below) — see the
resolution table. Re-evaluated against the spec/core/code.md §8.10
kind-shift lock (`:using` may return any kind regardless of focus kind);
that lock was always independent of this set.

| Fixture | Resolution (2026-05-30) |
|---|---|
| `program-modify-001-set-attribute` | ✅ supported. Under design (a) `/@name` is the `name` *attribute* of `user[= $_@id 1]`; `[set "Alicia"]` creates it → `[user id=1 name=Alicia [name Alice]]`. The `[name Alice]` child is element-axis and invisible to `/@name`. Fixture out_text updated to impl output. |
| `program-modify-003-original-unchanged` | ✅ supported. Rewritten to an attribute-based doc (`[users [user name=Alice]]`); `$orig/user@name` vs `$new/user@name` demonstrate immutability under design (a). Surfaced + fixed a §6.2 bug: a single-focus pure-child-chain terminal `@attr` now unwraps to the scalar value-as-string (`vcx/code/eval.v` walk_binding_path_seq; spec §6.2 "Terminal attribute unwrap"). |
| `program-modify-009-pipeline-multi-step` | ✅ supported. Rewritten to an attribute-based doc; `[@name="Bob"]` matches the `name` attribute and `[delete-attr email]` removes the `email` attribute, preserving the pipeline-multi-step coverage under design (a). |

**Attribute-axis lock (2026-05-30, design (a)).** The CXPath attribute axis
is name-disjoint from the element axes: `@name` / `/@name` match the `name`
*attribute* only; `/name` // `//name` match `name` *elements* only — they
never overlap, and a child element never falls through to an attribute step
(or vice-versa). This was previously an open spec follow-up; it is now the
locked semantics and the three fixtures above are conformant under it.
2. ~~`to-int` builtin (blocks 005). Either add `to-int` to the v0.8.0
   built-in set or rewrite fixture 005 to use a builtin already in
   scope (e.g. element-arithmetic that doesn't require explicit
   `to-int`).~~ **Resolved 2026-05-23 (task #42)** — v0.8.0 ships a
   generic `cast` builtin (`[cast value :type-tag]`, see §6.5) in
   lieu of a `to-int` / `to-float` family. Fixture 005 rewritten to
   `[* [cast $p :int] 2]` and un-deferred.
3. ~~Renderer string-quoting drift (blocks 007, 008).~~ **Resolved
   2026-05-23 (task #43)** — `vcx/code/render.v::render_body_item`
   now emits TextNode element-body children with quote wrappers
   regardless of bareword-safety, matching the long-standing
   'always-quote string bodies' convention already used for
   ScalarNode-typed string scalars. The cx-data parser collapses
   `[label 'Click me']` and `[label Click me]` to the same TextNode
   shape; the programs renderer now consistently emits the quoted
   surface for either input. Fixture `out_text` for modify-002 /
   004 / 006 / 007 / 008 was updated to the canonical quoted form
   in the same commit (data-equivalent on re-parse). A new fixture
   `program-modify-string-scalar-roundtrip` locks the round-trip
   contract — quotes survive `[?modify]` regardless of bareword-
   safety.

Once the attribute-axis-vs-child-element semantics land (item 1
above, also addressed at the spec level by commit
`ad5a00c5` — V impl needs to honor the rule), all three remaining
deferred fixtures (001 / 003 / 009) become ready-for-impl. None
are blocked on the §8.10 question addressed by this lock.

## Fixtures (core — `[?def]` module-level static functions per `spec/core/code.md` §8.7)

These fixtures cover the eight `[?def]` gates (34.1–34.8). They
exercise `[?def]` parse, no-overloading, two-pass load semantics,
argument shapes, bare-name references, `:scope` visibility, type-
expression grammar, and dev-strict validation.

Each fixture's `in_cx` is a placeholder `[doc]` because `[?def]` is
a module-level directive: the `in_code` block IS the module under
test. The runner is expected to evaluate the module and report its
last-expression value (or its declared `scope=public` exports) as
`out_text`.

**Implementation status:** the `[?def]` surface is specified; V
reference impl is Phase 2 work. These fixtures will FAIL until the
parser + evaluator land.
#]]
 ]

