 [; EBV unification (#383): owner ruling 2026-07-13 — the cxdm.md EBV table
    wins wholesale over code.md's old not() prose row. (1) A present named
    element is TRUTHY regardless of contents (node presence, XPath-style) —
    presence-vs-absence is the load-bearing distinction, and the existence-test
    idiom [?if //flag …] must hold for empty marker elements. (2) A singleton
    sequence wrapper RECURSES into its item — wrapping a value in a `(…)`
    singleton never changes its truth. Containers keep the empty-is-falsy
    convention ([] / {} falsy, non-empty truthy). Both eval truthiness sites
    (bare-operator dispatch and $-head/[?if]/guard dispatch) now share ONE
    EBV fn, so bare [not x] and [$not x] agree by construction. Non-scalar
    node kinds (text / comment / PI) are truthy by presence per the same
    node rule; no pure-CX pin exists for them because a bare text/comment/PI
    node is not constructable as a standalone condition value from program
    code — the arm is exercised structurally, like the NaN note above. ]

 [case id=program-if-elem-001-empty-elem-truthy level=core
  [tags control-flow if element ebv presence issue-383]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?if [flag] [then "present"] [else "absent"]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
'present'
#]]
 ]

