 [; Iterator EBV (#388): owner ruling 2026-07-13 — an Iterator in a boolean
    position has NO EBV and raises a LOUD, catchable CXER0100 (the same code
    family as materializing an unbounded iterator without a bound). EBV must
    never force a lazy stream: network-backed source kinds (net_accept /
    http_accept / sse_events / net_line / net_chunk) would block or perform
    I/O inside a condition, and combinator kinds run user closures per pull.
    Presence-truthy and silent-falsy were both rejected (wrapper-changes-
    truth incoherence / the #382 silent-surprise class). The error flows
    through both channels — err VALUE at value positions, EvalError at
    predicate walks — and [?fallback] catches either. A FINITE [$range] is
    an eager Sequence, not an Iterator, and keeps its ordinary sequence EBV. ]

 [case id=program-if-iter-001-open-range-err level=core
  [tags control-flow if iterator ebv error issue-388]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?if [$range 1 *] [then "t"] [else "f"]]
#]]
  [out-err [#
cx-err:CXER0100
#]]
 ]

